WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:02.225
- You kind of really

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.228
have blinders on

00:00:03.228 --> 00:00:06.831
and don't let yourself become comfortable

00:00:06.831 --> 00:00:08.256
and play it safe.

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:10.077
You can't take on a job because

00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:10.910
oh, well, what am I,

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.875
well, this has got to be a good one.

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:14.809
You have to just always go by your gut.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:16.122
- She an American actress,

00:00:16.122 --> 00:00:17.984
producer, and businesswoman.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.189
She gained worldwide fame

00:00:19.189 --> 00:00:20.666
for playing Rachel Green

00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:22.808
on the TV sitcom Friends.

00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:24.398
She's one of the highest paid actresses

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:25.277
in Hollywood.

00:00:25.277 --> 00:00:26.182
She's Jennifer Aniston

00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:27.409
and here's my take on her

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:29.294
top ten rules for success.

00:00:29.294 --> 00:00:30.651
Rule number two is my personal favorite,

00:00:30.651 --> 00:00:31.484
and make sure to stick around

00:00:31.484 --> 00:00:32.396
all the way to the end

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:33.789
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:35.044
Also, as Jennifer is talking,

00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:35.877
if she says something

00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:37.051
that really resonates with you,

00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:38.590
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.587
and put quotes around it

00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:41.203
so that other people can be inspired.

00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:42.973
And also, when you write it down,

00:00:42.973 --> 00:00:44.119
it's much more likely to stick

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:45.275
in your head, too.

00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:46.803
Enjoy.

00:00:46.803 --> 00:00:49.748
(electronic whooshing)

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:52.498
(dramatic music)

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.564
I think I was getting stuck myself,

00:01:01.564 --> 00:01:03.745
feeling nervous to take a chance and

00:01:03.745 --> 00:01:06.456
forgetting the fact that I'm an actor

00:01:06.456 --> 00:01:08.207
and I can play different parts

00:01:08.207 --> 00:01:09.412
and I've been on,

00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:10.821
I used to do character shows

00:01:10.821 --> 00:01:11.934
or sketch comedy shows

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.651
where I would do hundreds of characters.

00:01:13.651 --> 00:01:15.366
And all of sudden you get very safe

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:17.754
and very, you can feel stuck.

00:01:17.754 --> 00:01:18.816
And not only do you feel stuck,

00:01:18.816 --> 00:01:20.342
but the world

00:01:20.342 --> 00:01:22.296
sort of sticks you somewhere.

00:01:22.296 --> 00:01:23.516
They put you in a little box

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.473
and in a category.

00:01:24.473 --> 00:01:25.306
And so,

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.694
what I learned from it was don't listen.

00:01:29.694 --> 00:01:32.489
You got to really have blinders on,

00:01:32.489 --> 00:01:35.296
and don't let yourself become

00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:38.109
comfortable and play it safe

00:01:38.109 --> 00:01:38.946
'cause you'll burn out.

00:01:38.946 --> 00:01:40.522
And I want to do this for a while.

00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:43.115
I want to be around for
a little while longer.

00:01:43.115 --> 00:01:44.201
- [Interviewer] When
a script comes to you,

00:01:44.201 --> 00:01:45.435
when somebody's sending you a script,

00:01:45.435 --> 00:01:47.569
what, are you looking character first?

00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:48.683
Are you looking story first?

00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:50.254
Are you looking for the
whole project and how?

00:01:50.254 --> 00:01:53.013
- The whole kit and caboodle.

00:01:53.013 --> 00:01:55.974
I'd say the character, the story,

00:01:55.974 --> 00:01:59.193
and am I going to have a really good time?

00:01:59.193 --> 00:02:01.112
Am I going to connect to it?

00:02:01.112 --> 00:02:02.889
Doesn't have to be real serious or this.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.972
Could be a big blockbuster hit comedy

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.275
and I just want it to be really fun

00:02:09.275 --> 00:02:10.442
and enjoyable.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:12.642
The outcome's always going to be,

00:02:12.642 --> 00:02:14.541
you never know what the
outcomes going to be.

00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:15.851
And you can't do it for...

00:02:15.851 --> 00:02:17.362
You can't take on a job because,

00:02:17.362 --> 00:02:18.213
oh, well what am I,

00:02:18.213 --> 00:02:20.084
well, this has got to be a good one.

00:02:20.084 --> 00:02:21.604
You have to just always go by your gut

00:02:21.604 --> 00:02:23.076
and if you're going to enjoy yourself

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.471
and have good time creatively.

00:02:25.471 --> 00:02:26.734
And work with people.

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:29.659
Time saver: don't work with angry people.

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:31.863
Don't work with pain in the ass actors.

00:02:31.863 --> 00:02:33.787
Don't work with, you know,

00:02:33.787 --> 00:02:36.034
get all your information and say,

00:02:36.034 --> 00:02:37.823
yeah, life's too short rule.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:38.889
That falls under that.

00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:40.139
I will move on.

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:41.910
- You and I both believe

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.422
that you call things into your life.

00:02:44.422 --> 00:02:45.255
- Yes.

00:02:45.255 --> 00:02:46.650
- And that things happen as they should

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.554
when you're ready for it to happen.

00:02:49.554 --> 00:02:50.387
- That's right.

00:02:50.387 --> 00:02:51.220
The other day,

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.233
I was doing yoga with my girlfriend.

00:02:54.233 --> 00:02:57.118
And we finished, and we
were sort of sitting there

00:02:57.118 --> 00:02:58.984
just sort of stretching.

00:02:58.984 --> 00:03:00.367
And I looked over at her and I said,

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.350
you know what, I have to say

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.895
I'm feeling a feeling I have,

00:03:02.895 --> 00:03:05.645
I don't know if I've actually felt before.

00:03:05.645 --> 00:03:06.540
And that is

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.441
that I don't want to by anywhere other

00:03:10.441 --> 00:03:12.710
than where I am right now.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.824
Sitting across from you.

00:03:13.824 --> 00:03:16.597
(audience applauds)

00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:17.764
And that means

00:03:20.745 --> 00:03:23.726
I'm not sitting somewhere
dwelling on the past

00:03:23.726 --> 00:03:25.054
or I'm not fretting or obsessing

00:03:25.054 --> 00:03:27.612
about something in the future

00:03:27.612 --> 00:03:28.830
or something that was...

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.100
You know, it was just a
feeling of total peace.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.433
And I love that.

00:03:34.748 --> 00:03:36.195
- Well how did you get there?

00:03:36.195 --> 00:03:38.084
'Cause you had to shed some tears.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:38.917
You had to have some moments.

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:39.843
- Well, sure.

00:03:39.843 --> 00:03:40.951
- [Oprah] Where you
thought, like, oh my god.

00:03:40.951 --> 00:03:41.784
- Me not shed a tear?

00:03:41.784 --> 00:03:42.617
Come on.

00:03:42.617 --> 00:03:43.450
- [Oprah] Yeah, please, yeah.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.659
- So you know, although I did not

00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:46.434
burst into tears at the
opening of that article

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:47.267
by the way, I'll just say that.

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.184
But anyway.

00:03:49.435 --> 00:03:50.472
- [Oprah] So you shed some tears?

00:03:50.472 --> 00:03:51.385
- So I shed some tears,

00:03:51.385 --> 00:03:52.492
but meaning, you know,

00:03:52.492 --> 00:03:55.742
it's sort of that living in the moment.

00:03:56.675 --> 00:03:58.743
In the now as they say.

00:03:58.743 --> 00:04:00.336
And all the self-help books,

00:04:00.336 --> 00:04:01.712
'cause if I had a dollar for every book

00:04:01.712 --> 00:04:02.951
that was sent my way.

00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:04.270
(audience laughs)

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:05.918
I could have probably
paid for this studio.

00:04:05.918 --> 00:04:06.824
(audience laughs)

00:04:06.824 --> 00:04:07.950
You know.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.150
- You would have needed
two dollars for that.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.464
- [Jennifer] Two dollars for every book?

00:04:11.464 --> 00:04:14.464
(audience applauds)

00:04:15.474 --> 00:04:17.066
- [Oprah] Two dollars for every book.

00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:19.800
But yeah, you can read the books.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.082
- You can read them and you can sort of

00:04:21.082 --> 00:04:23.244
intellectualize it, but the truth is,

00:04:23.244 --> 00:04:24.110
and you sit there going,

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.583
well how do I do that.

00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:27.456
And you're frustrated
and then you get down

00:04:27.456 --> 00:04:29.422
on yourself because you're not there yet.

00:04:29.422 --> 00:04:31.423
And then you just realized one day

00:04:31.423 --> 00:04:32.760
it's just happened.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.293
It's collected in your, you know,

00:04:34.293 --> 00:04:36.704
your cellular memory.

00:04:36.704 --> 00:04:38.745
And then one day you're sitting there

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.289
with your friend doing yoga and you go,

00:04:40.289 --> 00:04:41.501
oh, I get it.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:42.334
- [Oprah] I'm okay.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:43.167
- I get it.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.858
You know, we all have
varying degrees of loss

00:04:44.858 --> 00:04:47.582
and sadness and pain in our lives,

00:04:47.582 --> 00:04:49.918
and it's a necessity honestly

00:04:49.918 --> 00:04:51.356
'cause then how would we appreciate

00:04:51.356 --> 00:04:54.313
the good times and the hopeful times

00:04:54.313 --> 00:04:57.947
and all of the abundance that life has

00:04:57.947 --> 00:04:59.780
if you go and grab it.

00:05:01.147 --> 00:05:02.983
But it's a personal choice

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:04.733
to get up and move on

00:05:05.757 --> 00:05:06.924
and be better.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:10.023
I was saying the other day to somebody,

00:05:10.023 --> 00:05:11.708
I think all actors

00:05:11.708 --> 00:05:12.998
who are maybe

00:05:12.998 --> 00:05:14.831
gratefully, successful

00:05:16.772 --> 00:05:19.911
sometimes, if you are identified

00:05:19.911 --> 00:05:21.171
with something like Friends,

00:05:21.171 --> 00:05:23.263
you almost feel like you're an actor

00:05:23.263 --> 00:05:25.615
in a closet always trying like...

00:05:25.615 --> 00:05:27.841
I want to do more, you know what I mean?

00:05:27.841 --> 00:05:29.741
And it's always,

00:05:29.741 --> 00:05:31.034
there's always a little bit

00:05:31.034 --> 00:05:33.225
of a struggle and a challenge.

00:05:33.225 --> 00:05:34.479
But I find that exciting,

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:36.317
you know what I mean?

00:05:36.317 --> 00:05:38.150
To keep pushing myself

00:05:39.291 --> 00:05:41.065
and to keep challenging myself

00:05:41.065 --> 00:05:42.361
and taking risks.

00:05:42.361 --> 00:05:44.291
I think it's important not to get lazy

00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:45.801
and stay safe.

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:46.695
You have to understand,

00:05:46.695 --> 00:05:48.422
when you have nothing to compare it to,

00:05:48.422 --> 00:05:50.189
and you just get to go to work

00:05:50.189 --> 00:05:51.623
and you see so many of your friends

00:05:51.623 --> 00:05:52.971
who are not working,

00:05:52.971 --> 00:05:55.554
I'm just grateful to be working

00:05:57.034 --> 00:05:58.968
and doing movies

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:01.222
that I found fun and entertaining.

00:06:01.222 --> 00:06:03.812
And some were beloved and some were not.

00:06:03.812 --> 00:06:06.255
You know, and then it
wasn't until I got really,

00:06:06.255 --> 00:06:09.151
starting getting older where I realized

00:06:09.151 --> 00:06:11.943
I think having done The Good Girl,

00:06:11.943 --> 00:06:14.026
it made me really sort of

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:18.655
realize, oh, I have a
choice of what I can do.

00:06:18.655 --> 00:06:21.543
I really can explore other things

00:06:21.543 --> 00:06:23.920
and not just sit back and just wait

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.807
for what's handed to you.

00:06:25.807 --> 00:06:28.735
So I think I started back then making

00:06:28.735 --> 00:06:31.220
being more conscious and vocal

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.131
with my managers and agents about stuff.

00:06:35.131 --> 00:06:37.296
Areas that I wanted to explore.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.429
- You know, you've been
into yoga for years

00:06:38.429 --> 00:06:39.671
and you also meditate.

00:06:39.671 --> 00:06:40.504
- [Jennifer] Yes.

00:06:40.504 --> 00:06:41.560
- So what are some of the biggest changes

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.220
that that has brought to your life?

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.053
- You know,

00:06:45.053 --> 00:06:47.950
it's kind of not one thing

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:50.118
you can point at or put a finger on.

00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:51.918
It's just...

00:06:51.918 --> 00:06:54.335
I can tell you that I feel...

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.052
It's like a kick start for your day.

00:06:58.052 --> 00:06:59.048
It just centers you.

00:06:59.048 --> 00:06:59.965
And things,

00:07:01.078 --> 00:07:03.862
your stress levels are just down.

00:07:03.862 --> 00:07:06.764
And you find yourself
interacting in the world

00:07:06.764 --> 00:07:08.355
much easier and better,

00:07:08.355 --> 00:07:10.022
and in a calmer way.

00:07:11.963 --> 00:07:13.836
And there's just a peaceful joy

00:07:13.836 --> 00:07:14.899
that sort of comes over.

00:07:14.899 --> 00:07:15.757
And you can't,

00:07:15.757 --> 00:07:17.191
I don't know how or why,

00:07:17.191 --> 00:07:18.687
it's no rhyme or reason.

00:07:18.687 --> 00:07:20.611
And I just know that if I,

00:07:20.611 --> 00:07:23.602
if I go through a phase where I slip off

00:07:23.602 --> 00:07:25.907
and I'm not as religious with it,

00:07:25.907 --> 00:07:27.639
I feel the difference.

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:28.550
I just feel it.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.497
- Yeah, and for people

00:07:29.497 --> 00:07:30.818
that are maybe a little bit intimidated

00:07:30.818 --> 00:07:31.913
about taking up meditation,

00:07:31.913 --> 00:07:33.207
what can you tell them?

00:07:33.207 --> 00:07:36.282
- Just, there's nothing to do wrong.

00:07:36.282 --> 00:07:38.115
You can't do it wrong.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.239
You could go take a class if you want.

00:07:42.239 --> 00:07:43.082
You can have someone come

00:07:43.082 --> 00:07:45.608
to give you training in it.

00:07:45.608 --> 00:07:47.419
Or you can just find something

00:07:47.419 --> 00:07:48.252
that works for you.

00:07:48.252 --> 00:07:49.846
You can just listen to beautiful music

00:07:49.846 --> 00:07:53.429
and just find gratitude
in whatever is here

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:57.007
or in what you have.

00:07:59.997 --> 00:08:02.732
All I can say is you can't mess it up.

00:08:02.732 --> 00:08:04.442
- Have you ever again, no names.

00:08:04.442 --> 00:08:05.275
- No names.

00:08:05.275 --> 00:08:06.592
- But have you ever accepted a project

00:08:06.592 --> 00:08:08.149
and then been into it a couple of weeks,

00:08:08.149 --> 00:08:10.933
and said, not to the world and not to me,

00:08:10.933 --> 00:08:12.043
but to your best friend,

00:08:12.043 --> 00:08:14.782
oh, I don't think this is

00:08:14.782 --> 00:08:16.643
what I expected it to be.

00:08:16.643 --> 00:08:18.082
- Yes I have.

00:08:18.082 --> 00:08:19.915
(audience laughs)

00:08:19.915 --> 00:08:21.413
- [Interviewer] All right, so now,

00:08:21.413 --> 00:08:23.289
no names was our deal, but...

00:08:23.289 --> 00:08:25.031
- Like I'm going to actually name a name.

00:08:25.031 --> 00:08:25.959
(audience laughs)

00:08:25.959 --> 00:08:28.126
That would just not happen.

00:08:28.126 --> 00:08:29.088
- [Interviewer] But how do you

00:08:29.088 --> 00:08:29.921
get through that then?

00:08:29.921 --> 00:08:30.754
- How do you get through it?

00:08:30.754 --> 00:08:31.587
You have to do...

00:08:31.587 --> 00:08:32.420
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
'cause you're three weeks

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.253
into it and then you've got another

00:08:33.253 --> 00:08:34.938
three or four or six weeks of shooting.

00:08:34.938 --> 00:08:36.240
- You make the best of it.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.975
You just take care of your job.

00:08:37.975 --> 00:08:39.188
You know, and you talk

00:08:39.188 --> 00:08:40.926
and you have as much of a dialogue

00:08:40.926 --> 00:08:42.899
with them as you possibly can.

00:08:42.899 --> 00:08:45.649
And, you know, just get in there.

00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:47.608
Get very involved.

00:08:47.608 --> 00:08:48.821
Sometimes you can just sit back

00:08:48.821 --> 00:08:50.925
and you can just do your job.

00:08:50.925 --> 00:08:54.752
And sometimes it's
important that you kind of

00:08:54.752 --> 00:08:57.230
be a bit more collaborative, you know.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.057
I was always a yo yo dieter.

00:08:59.057 --> 00:09:01.150
I was a chubbier kid.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.671
- But did you do drastic things to diet?

00:09:02.671 --> 00:09:03.623
- No.

00:09:03.623 --> 00:09:06.613
Was I just bulimic or anorexic?

00:09:06.613 --> 00:09:08.946
No, but I was a diet-aholic.

00:09:10.744 --> 00:09:12.491
Definitely.

00:09:12.491 --> 00:09:13.550
Grapefruit diet I remember.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.764
There was the watermelon diet.

00:09:14.764 --> 00:09:17.755
There was the white grain of rice diet.

00:09:17.755 --> 00:09:19.409
- [Press] Jennifer.

00:09:19.409 --> 00:09:20.242
- [Interviewer] But these days

00:09:20.242 --> 00:09:21.080
she says it's different.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.162
She works out three to four days a week

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:24.241
and has learned to make eating

00:09:24.241 --> 00:09:25.513
about life now,

00:09:25.513 --> 00:09:27.956
not a reaction to the past.

00:09:27.956 --> 00:09:29.627
A father who broke up the family

00:09:29.627 --> 00:09:31.747
and a volatile mother.

00:09:31.747 --> 00:09:33.874
- I want to say to all these young girls

00:09:33.874 --> 00:09:36.249
there are so many struggles
that everybody has,

00:09:36.249 --> 00:09:37.306
especially when it's like

00:09:37.306 --> 00:09:38.330
you don't know what you're filling up.

